================================================================================
PYTHON LAYER
================================================================================

The phantom_frontmatter package has no third-party Python dependencies. It uses
only the standard library — argparse, json, logging, pathlib, subprocess,
ipaddress, secrets, dataclasses and the like.

  (none)

requirements.txt, which ships with the release, pins no packages; it is compiled
with hashes from requirements.in, which declares none. The interpreter is the
distribution's own python3, installed from apt; see SYSTEM PACKAGES below.

================================================================================
BUNDLED BINARIES — WSTUNNEL
================================================================================

wstunnel is the only third-party binary this package redistributes. It is the
WebSocket/TLS tunnel server that Ghost Mode clients connect to: it carries
opaque UDP datagrams inside a WebSocket over TLS, so the tunnel survives
networks that block or filter UDP.

