CI workflow: https://github.com/ARAS-Workspace/wstunnel/actions/runs/36175403584

Shipped inside this package, both architectures:

  phantom_frontmatter/bin/lib/wstunnel_<VERSION>_linux_amd64.tar.gz
  phantom_frontmatter/bin/lib/wstunnel_<VERSION>_linux_arm64.tar.gz
  phantom_frontmatter/bin/lib/checksums.txt   sha256sums from the release
  phantom_frontmatter/bin/lib/README          provenance for the tarballs

VERSION above is the version in the table, pinned in code at
phantom_frontmatter/modules/setup/lib/binary_utils.py. That module also performs
the extraction: `frontmatter-api setup init` unpacks the tarball matching the
host's architecture.

Usage Note:
Nothing here is fetched at run time. The tarballs travel inside the release, so
neither installation nor operation reaches out to GitHub. frontmatter-update.sh
replaces phantom_frontmatter/ from the new release and swaps the wstunnel binary
only when the bundled version changed; it makes no network request of its own.

